Getting Started Tips
Your Learning Path
1
Start with Minikube (Local Kubernetes)
Install Minikube on your laptop. It's a single-node cluster perfect for learning.

2
Learn kubectl Commands
Master the basics: get, describe, logs, exec, create, delete. Practice daily!

3
Deploy Simple Apps First
Start with nginx or a "Hello World" app. Don't jump to complex microservices yet.

4
Understand YAML Files
Everything in Kubernetes is defined in YAML. Learn to read and write them.

5
Practice Debugging
Learn to troubleshoot with: kubectl logs, kubectl describe, kubectl get events.

